NAME
       nl - number lines of files

SYNOPSIS
       nl [-b a|t|n] [-v N] [-i N] [-w N] [-s SEP] [FILE]...

DESCRIPTION
       Write each FILE to standard output with line numbers added.

OPTIONS
       -b STYLE
           a: number all lines, t: nonempty lines (default), n: no lines

       -v N
           first line number

       -i N
           line number increment

       -w N
           width of line numbers

       -s SEP
           separator after the number

EXAMPLES
       nl main.c

SEE ALSO
       cat(1)
